  "rules": "Lava pours from the forge mouth S along the trunk channel and drains into the crevice in the east wall. Hot cells block you. Push a cooling stone into the trunk to dam it: every trunk cell below the dam cools (walkable) and the lava backs up into the side branches whose junction is above the dam, filling their heat basins. A filled basin latches its forge latch (u1-u3) for good. Stones in the trunk can only be pushed upstream, and a dam cannot be lifted out (you would be standing in the flow), so the first dam decides which basins fill. The bellows W1/W2 return both stones to their racks (latches stay lit); W1 sits in the east pocket so a bad dam never traps you. All three latches open the forge gates G1/G2; you still need a dam west of the gates to cross the trunk to the landing. Stones cannot be pushed onto the cinder grate in front of W1.",
  "solution": "Push the east rack stone up into the trunk at x14 (below every junction, so all three basins fill and latch), work the bellows W1, then push the west stone up into the trunk at x6: the trunk east of it cools and you walk up through the gates. See verified.shortest_solution.",
